1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,020
"Not Yours"

2
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,800
(Episode 8)

3
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:07,279
I haven't been back for a while.

4
00:01:07,359 --> 00:01:08,680
The house is lively again.

5
00:01:09,519 --> 00:01:11,279
Why didn't you tell me
you were coming back?

6
00:01:11,959 --> 00:01:13,640
I wanted to surprise you.

7
00:01:14,359 --> 00:01:16,319
Instead, you ended up
giving me a huge surprise.

8
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:21,159
With so many people in the house,

9
00:01:21,239 --> 00:01:22,840
which one is your new favorite?

10
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:27,560
A Pong and Milan will be
joining my company soon.

11
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:30,040
They'll be making money
for you in the future.

12
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:33,040
So the one you slept with

13
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:35,439
is the boy you carried home last time?

14
00:01:35,519 --> 00:01:36,896
Didn't you hear everything just now?

15
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:37,920
Why bother asking?

16
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:40,879
Well, you're young.

17
00:01:40,959 --> 00:01:44,000
It's normal to have desires and
let off some steam occasionally.

18
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:46,279
However, I heard

19
00:01:46,359 --> 00:01:48,319
you haven't been going
to the office much lately.

20
00:01:49,439 --> 00:01:51,799
Did you check last
quarter's financial report?

21
00:01:51,879 --> 00:01:54,280
Haven't you been neglecting
the company for a while?

22
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:57,736
And what about that in-house
variety show you mentioned?

23
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:59,160
Why hasn't there been any progress?

24
00:02:00,719 --> 00:02:03,560
Milan is the one I picked
to be the guest on the show.

25
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,415
Even though he's in a dispute
to terminate his contract,

26
00:02:06,439 --> 00:02:07,439
to be honest,

27
00:02:08,319 --> 00:02:10,559
plenty of agencies in
Tailan want to work with him.

28
00:02:10,639 --> 00:02:13,040
To win him over, you have to
win over the people around him

29
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,240
and bring his team on board.

30
00:02:14,919 --> 00:02:16,320
If he agrees to join us,

31
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:18,320
our show won't have to
worry about getting buzz.

32
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:20,080
Good.

33
00:02:20,159 --> 00:02:21,520
You didn't let me down after all.

34
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:25,320
So, can you lock Milan down?

35
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:26,639
Can we sign him smoothly?

36
00:02:27,159 --> 00:02:28,159
No problem.

37
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,239
Well,

38
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:33,319
that's good.

39
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,440
Since you can sign him,

40
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:39,200
keep your hands off the people around him.

41
00:02:39,639 --> 00:02:41,000
Those boys of yours,

42
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:42,240
give it a rest.

43
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:48,360
What's that weird smell on you?

44
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:51,639
People of our status

45
00:02:51,719 --> 00:02:53,519
must smell fresh at all times.

46
00:02:53,599 --> 00:02:56,240
It probably got on me
while I was making breakfast.

47
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:59,519
You didn't just make breakfast,

48
00:02:59,599 --> 00:03:00,960
you even ate with them?

49
00:03:01,919 --> 00:03:03,920
I came today to remind you

50
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,360
that this is the last time.

51
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:09,159
Stop bringing random strangers
into the house from now on.

52
00:03:09,879 --> 00:03:11,520
They leave the stench
of poverty behind.

53
00:03:22,439 --> 00:03:23,679
See?

54
00:03:23,759 --> 00:03:25,479
This is the scent that suits you.

55
00:03:27,919 --> 00:03:28,919
To me,

56
00:03:31,039 --> 00:03:32,039
he's not a stranger.

57
00:03:34,759 --> 00:03:36,840
So you're dead set on dating him?

58
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:40,479
Just like that last one.

59
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:43,680
What was his name again?

60
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:46,800
Taozi?

61
00:03:47,639 --> 00:03:48,639
Yes.

62
00:03:49,159 --> 00:03:50,280
But please call him Pao Bei.

63
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,680
He's not that person from before.

64
00:03:53,159 --> 00:03:54,919
Please don't bring up irrelevant people.

65
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:57,360
What's the difference?

66
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:00,679
Even if their backgrounds are different,

67
00:04:00,759 --> 00:04:01,759
it will end the same way.

68
00:04:03,319 --> 00:04:05,440
Don't tell me you've
forgotten about the agreement

69
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,320
you signed when Father passed away.

70
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,840
It's legally binding.

71
00:04:09,919 --> 00:04:11,679
If you insist on being with him...

72
00:04:11,759 --> 00:04:12,759
Don't worry.

73
00:04:13,319 --> 00:04:14,959
I won't let it get in the way of my work.

74
00:04:15,719 --> 00:04:17,016
Whether I'm just fooling around with him

75
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,400
or in it for the long haul,

76
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:19,480
it's my business.

77
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Besides,

78
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:25,040
I don't really care about that agreement.

79
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:28,639
Right now, I just want to follow my heart.

80
00:04:30,199 --> 00:04:32,040
If I really breach the contract one day

81
00:04:33,399 --> 00:04:34,920
and you want to take away my assets,

82
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,000
go right ahead.

83
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,480
That'll just be my fate.

84
00:04:47,519 --> 00:04:48,640
What is it?

85
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,879
Mr. Pao Bei has changed
back into his own clothes

86
00:04:50,959 --> 00:04:53,119
and left with Mr. A Pong.

87
00:04:53,199 --> 00:04:55,319
They saw you were busy
and didn't want to bother you,

88
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:56,680
so they asked me to let you know.

89
00:04:57,480 --> 00:05:00,879
Also, regarding the meeting
on Mr. Milan's contract,

90
00:05:00,959 --> 00:05:03,160
the legal team would like
to meet with you privately.

91
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,360
Tell Legal to wait for me at the office.

92
00:05:06,839 --> 00:05:09,279
And the meeting with
the show's director today,

93
00:05:09,839 --> 00:05:11,456
that's scheduled at the office too, right?

94
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:12,319
Yes, Young Master.

95
00:05:12,399 --> 00:05:13,399
Okay.

96
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:19,359
You see,

97
00:05:19,439 --> 00:05:20,679
I still have a lot on my plate.

98
00:05:21,279 --> 00:05:22,400
So, brother,

99
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:24,640
I won't be staying home to
have a meal with you today.

100
00:05:25,639 --> 00:05:27,279
Oh, and one more thing.

101
00:05:28,279 --> 00:05:30,720
Give me a heads-up before
you come back next time.

102
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:34,120
In case it turns out to be a
shock instead of a surprise,

103
00:05:34,759 --> 00:05:37,720
for someone like you
who prefers a quiet life,

104
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:39,080
it would be torture,

105
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:40,160
wouldn't it?

106
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:55,879
This is your scent.

107
00:05:55,959 --> 00:05:56,959
I'm not a fan of it.

108
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:09,160
Is this scent a bit too strong?

109
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:11,759
Can I be honest?

110
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:13,879
Go ahead.

111
00:06:13,959 --> 00:06:15,519
It doesn't really suit your vibe.

112
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:17,480
What's my vibe?

113
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,839
Actually, you come across as quite warm,

114
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:23,040
but this scent is way too cold.

115
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:27,640
That's the first time
anyone has called me warm.

116
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:29,440
People usually say I'm pretty intimidating.

117
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:33,199
Well, the way you lost your
temper and yelled earlier,

118
00:06:34,079 --> 00:06:36,680
that was indeed a bit scary.

119
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:43,320
The two of us were just joking around.

120
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:44,640
Who the hell is joking with you?

121
00:06:44,959 --> 00:06:46,159
Are you messing with me again?

122
00:06:47,279 --> 00:06:49,439
Did I really scare him?

123
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:53,720
Honestly, you scared me too.

124
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:56,879
Was it really that bad?

125
00:06:58,439 --> 00:06:59,679
It wasn't that bad, was it?

126
00:06:59,759 --> 00:07:01,560
I'm not talking about your attitude.

127
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,959
I mean what you said earlier

128
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:07,040
about the two of you sleeping together.

129
00:07:07,319 --> 00:07:08,480
That can't be true, right?

130
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:11,495
You guys were just putting on an act.

131
00:07:11,519 --> 00:07:12,720
It was a joke, right?

132
00:07:17,079 --> 00:07:18,239
You really did sleep together...?

133
00:07:23,399 --> 00:07:24,759
What's wrong?

134
00:07:24,839 --> 00:07:27,439
Do you think Pao Bei
wouldn't like someone like me?

135
00:07:27,519 --> 00:07:28,519
Of course not.

136
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,600
For someone as outstanding as you,

137
00:07:30,639 --> 00:07:32,920
it's only natural for people to like you.

138
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:34,639
It's just that...

139
00:07:36,066 --> 00:07:37,066
"It's just that..."?

140
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:40,720
Or do you think I wouldn't like Pao Bei?

141
00:07:43,519 --> 00:07:44,519
Not that either.

142
00:07:45,199 --> 00:07:46,240
Pao Bei is adorable.

143
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:48,560
I like him a lot too.

144
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,560
What do you like about him?

145
00:07:52,839 --> 00:07:53,920
He's kind,

146
00:07:55,519 --> 00:07:56,519
hardworking,

147
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:58,680
and very simple.

148
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:01,079
Just like...

149
00:08:03,519 --> 00:08:05,199
Just like the grass on the ground.

150
00:08:05,279 --> 00:08:07,399
No matter how barren the environment is,

151
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:09,360
as long as there's a ray of sunshine

152
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:11,279
and a drop of rain,

153
00:08:11,879 --> 00:08:13,359
it will seize the chance

154
00:08:13,439 --> 00:08:14,759
and grow tenaciously.

155
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:17,560
It doesn't ask for much,

156
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:21,120
yet it always gives life back to the world.

157
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,240
Since you and I are so in sync,

158
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:27,519
you must feel the same way, right?

159
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:33,000
I fully support the two
of you being together,

160
00:08:33,799 --> 00:08:36,879
and I think Pao Bei really likes you too.

161
00:08:39,039 --> 00:08:40,319
As an outsider,

162
00:08:40,399 --> 00:08:41,759
I can see it very clearly.

163
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:49,160
Well...

164
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,279
It's just a pity that

165
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:53,840
every time it feels like
we're making progress,

166
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:58,399
we end up having a
fight like the one just now.

167
00:09:03,039 --> 00:09:04,039
Are the two of us

168
00:09:06,919 --> 00:09:08,599
just not right for each other?

169
00:09:08,679 --> 00:09:10,519
No two people are born a perfect match.

170
00:09:13,279 --> 00:09:14,639
If you want it to last,

171
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,360
you have to learn to be
considerate of each other.

172
00:09:20,799 --> 00:09:21,960
I feel like

173
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,800
he doesn't plan on going
that far with me anyway.

174
00:09:25,559 --> 00:09:26,319
If I were him,

175
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:28,559
I wouldn't dare hope to
go too far with you either.

176
00:09:28,639 --> 00:09:31,000
After all, you're so high and mighty.

177
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,216
In his eyes, he must feel like

178
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:34,160
he's from a completely
different world than you.

179
00:09:34,799 --> 00:09:35,719
Of course,

180
00:09:35,799 --> 00:09:37,679
that's just how I see it.

181
00:09:37,759 --> 00:09:39,520
I think you could try talking to him

182
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:41,240
patiently and gently,

183
00:09:41,759 --> 00:09:43,159
just like how you're talking to me,

184
00:09:43,919 --> 00:09:45,440
and hear what he truly thinks.

185
00:09:46,519 --> 00:09:48,160
He already left with A Pong

186
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:49,519
without even saying goodbye.

187
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:51,600
Where am I supposed to find him?

188
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:54,159
When you really want to see someone,

189
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:56,120
you'll always find a way.

190
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:01,200
By the way,

191
00:10:01,879 --> 00:10:03,519
when they were leaving earlier,

192
00:10:04,039 --> 00:10:06,079
A Pong mentioned Pao
Bei's scooter is a bit old

193
00:10:06,159 --> 00:10:07,360
and hard to ride.

194
00:10:07,879 --> 00:10:09,960
I wonder if they made it home safely.

195
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:14,959
Young Master,

196
00:10:15,039 --> 00:10:16,160
it's almost time.

197
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,040
We should head out.

198
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:18,120
Okay.

199
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:21,480
I need you to do something for me later.

200
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:23,000
Yes, Young Master.

201
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,080
I'll take care of it.

202
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:37,720
Why are you staring at me?

203
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:41,880
Tell me.

204
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:44,040
I thought I knew you pretty well.

205
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:45,440
But now I realize.

206
00:10:46,039 --> 00:10:47,480
I barely recognize you anymore.

207
00:10:49,519 --> 00:10:50,600
What makes you say that?

208
00:10:52,559 --> 00:10:53,719
Be honest with me.

209
00:10:53,799 --> 00:10:56,360
Did that guy use your debt

210
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:57,720
to force you into bed with him?

211
00:11:00,279 --> 00:11:01,279
Of course not.

212
00:11:01,879 --> 00:11:03,239
Like I'd ever let anyone force me.

213
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:05,520
Pao Bei,

214
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:07,559
you're really playing the long game here.

215
00:11:07,639 --> 00:11:09,240
First, you win him over.

216
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:10,879
Make him fall head over heels for you.

217
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:13,519
Then, once you've had
your fun, you dump him hard.

218
00:11:14,279 --> 00:11:15,976
Last time he treated us
to the amusement park.

219
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,479
Where are we going next?

220
00:11:17,559 --> 00:11:18,799
How about a trip abroad?

221
00:11:28,799 --> 00:11:29,919
Wait, what's with that look?

222
00:11:30,399 --> 00:11:32,199
Don't tell me it's over
after just one night.

223
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:34,320
Are you tired of him already?

224
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:39,000
Actually, I'm seriously
considering dating him.

225
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:42,799
What?

226
00:11:42,879 --> 00:11:44,080
You actually like him?

227
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:48,120
Hold on.

228
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:51,440
How can you put up with
a guy like that long-term?

229
00:11:53,399 --> 00:11:55,559
I have my ways of handling him.

230
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:57,759
Like what?

231
00:12:01,159 --> 00:12:02,760
Why is this tiny thing so spicy?

232
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:03,840
Water!

233
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,240
Don't drink water,
it'll only make it worse.

234
00:12:08,879 --> 00:12:10,160
Chilies have capsaicin in them.

235
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:11,559
If you drink water,

236
00:12:11,639 --> 00:12:13,719
it just spreads the burn faster.

237
00:12:13,799 --> 00:12:15,440
It'll only make your mouth burn more.

238
00:12:16,639 --> 00:12:17,839
Milk.

239
00:12:17,919 --> 00:12:19,039
Here, drink this instead.

240
00:12:24,039 --> 00:12:25,480
Milk contains fat.

241
00:12:26,039 --> 00:12:28,000
The fat binds to the capsaicin

242
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,360
and dissolves it right away.

243
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,280
That stops the burning.

244
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:31,639
Yeah, I know that.

245
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:35,320
Why are you lecturing
me like a science teacher?

246
00:12:36,919 --> 00:12:38,360
Didn't you just ask how I'm going

247
00:12:39,679 --> 00:12:40,720
to handle him?

248
00:12:41,639 --> 00:12:42,919
If he's the chili pepper,

249
00:12:43,679 --> 00:12:44,720
and I'm the water,

250
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:47,039
it'll only backfire.

251
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,120
But if I'm the milk,

252
00:12:50,639 --> 00:12:52,759
I can neutralize his heat completely.

253
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:56,399
I only half-get what you're saying,

254
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,719
but it sounds pretty badass.

255
00:12:58,799 --> 00:13:00,159
I'm sticking with you from now on.

256
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:02,880
When you move into a big mansion,

257
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:04,840
don't forget your buddy A Pong.

258
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:08,839
A Pong,

259
00:13:08,919 --> 00:13:10,040
look who's talking.

260
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:12,360
Aren't you working for
a big movie star now?

261
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,839
Neither of us should be freeloaders.

262
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:17,640
Once you make it big in showbiz,

263
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:19,120
you can make me a star, too.

264
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:21,599
My gig is nowhere near as solid as yours.

265
00:13:21,679 --> 00:13:23,679
You're practically marrying into a dynasty.

266
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:27,919
If that's how you see it,

267
00:13:28,559 --> 00:13:29,976
you could always marry
into his family, too.

268
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,759
I think you and Milan
make a pretty good match.

269
00:13:34,279 --> 00:13:35,599
What are you talking about?

270
00:13:35,679 --> 00:13:36,759
Quit talking nonsense.

271
00:13:38,799 --> 00:13:41,160
Why aren't Xiaotong and Xiaoya back yet?

272
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:42,600
I'll go check on them.

273
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:54,840
We're here, Master.

274
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:09,840
Coming!

275
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,480
The Young Master wants to see you.

276
00:14:14,799 --> 00:14:15,879
Why'd you call me out here?

277
00:14:16,879 --> 00:14:18,040
Teach me how to ride this.

278
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:19,479
Don't you know how?

279
00:14:19,559 --> 00:14:20,920
Then how did you get it here?

280
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,280
You just can't go a single day

281
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,680
without messing with me, can you?

282
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:25,640
Mingkun gave me a ride.

283
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:26,599
If you teach me how to ride it,

284
00:14:26,679 --> 00:14:27,520
I'll give it to you.

285
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:28,679
It's brand new.

286
00:14:28,759 --> 00:14:30,280
Get Mingkun to teach you.

287
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,760
I'm not cut out to be your teacher.

288
00:14:36,039 --> 00:14:37,159
I only want you to teach me.

289
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,920
You have a perfectly good car.

290
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,400
Why do you even want to learn this?

291
00:14:43,519 --> 00:14:44,840
I want to

292
00:14:46,639 --> 00:14:48,080
get closer to your world.

293
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,600
What are you standing there for?

294
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:12,200
Let's go.

295
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:45,480
Be careful.

296
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:49,535
Watch where you're going! Are you blind?

297
00:15:49,559 --> 00:15:49,920
I'm sorry!

298
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,120
Some people have no manners.

299
00:16:01,879 --> 00:16:02,919
Nice job!

300
00:16:30,799 --> 00:16:32,079
Why are you sitting so far away?

301
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:34,000
Just trying not to overheat you.

302
00:16:34,759 --> 00:16:36,440
It's too hot to sit that close.

303
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:39,199
Come here.

304
00:16:39,279 --> 00:16:40,600
I like having you close to me.

305
00:17:08,519 --> 00:17:09,775
Why did you only buy one bottle?

306
00:17:09,799 --> 00:17:10,799
Aren't you thirsty?

307
00:17:11,519 --> 00:17:12,519
I'm not.

308
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:17,559
Oh, I get it.

309
00:17:19,599 --> 00:17:22,680
You wanted us to share
the same bottle, didn't you?

310
00:17:23,839 --> 00:17:25,440
Too bad I drank it all. Now what?

311
00:17:26,599 --> 00:17:27,639
I'll just buy another one.

312
00:17:30,519 --> 00:17:31,640
Stop wasting money.

313
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:34,200
I'll just drink some water when I get home.

314
00:17:35,079 --> 00:17:36,679
Did you need anything else?

315
00:17:36,759 --> 00:17:38,799
If not, I'm heading back.

316
00:17:41,799 --> 00:17:42,880
Wait, come back.

317
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:43,960
There is something.

318
00:17:51,599 --> 00:17:52,880
What is it?

319
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:55,640
I...

320
00:18:00,319 --> 00:18:01,400
I wanted to ask you,

321
00:18:02,119 --> 00:18:03,359
do you have any hobbies?

322
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:06,880
Not really.

323
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:07,960
None at all?

324
00:18:09,799 --> 00:18:11,240
Doesn't everyone have a hobby?

325
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:13,439
Take you, for example.

326
00:18:13,519 --> 00:18:14,679
Cooking is your hobby, right?

327
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:18,679
Cooking is just how I survive.

328
00:18:18,759 --> 00:18:20,039
It doesn't count as a hobby.

329
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,856
I'll teach you how to skateboard next time.

330
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:23,976
I might suck at riding a scooter,

331
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,359
but I'm amazing on a skateboard.

332
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,360
You need to pick up some hobbies.

333
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:31,160
Life's way too boring without them.

334
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:36,439
Poor people don't have the energy

335
00:18:36,519 --> 00:18:38,920
to waste on useless hobbies.

336
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:44,359
Just scraping by is hard enough.

337
00:18:47,039 --> 00:18:49,720
That's why you should just be with me.

338
00:18:53,279 --> 00:18:54,519
Hear me out first.

339
00:18:55,680 --> 00:18:57,519
Even if I do end up with you,

340
00:18:57,599 --> 00:18:59,439
it'll be because I like you,

341
00:18:59,519 --> 00:19:00,559
not because of your money.

342
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:03,279
Then...

343
00:19:03,359 --> 00:19:05,759
when you said we were just
in it for the physical pleasure,

344
00:19:05,839 --> 00:19:06,839
did you mean it?

345
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:12,376
I only said that because you're always
flying off the handle for no reason.

346
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:15,012
I wasn't flying off the handle!
I just panicked, that's all.

347
00:19:15,079 --> 00:19:15,999
Then can you promise me

348
00:19:16,079 --> 00:19:17,439
you'll stop acting like that?

349
00:19:17,519 --> 00:19:19,920
Stop losing your temper out of nowhere

350
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:21,719
and resorting to violence.

351
00:19:21,799 --> 00:19:23,015
Can we just talk things
through like normal people?

352
00:19:23,039 --> 00:19:23,840
Hold on.

353
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:25,616
Doesn't your friend lose
his temper all the time?

354
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:26,656
Why don't you lecture him?

355
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:27,279
He even punched me!

356
00:19:27,359 --> 00:19:28,959
That's totally different.

357
00:19:29,039 --> 00:19:30,239
He was acting in self-defense.

358
00:19:30,279 --> 00:19:31,039
He was just having my back.

359
00:19:31,119 --> 00:19:32,216
You, on the other hand,
are completely unreasonable.

360
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:33,320
You lash out at everything.

361
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:35,279
If you keep doing that,

362
00:19:35,359 --> 00:19:36,519
it's honestly going to make

363
00:19:36,599 --> 00:19:37,719
being around you exhausting.

364
00:19:53,759 --> 00:19:54,759
Have a seat.

365
00:19:56,759 --> 00:19:58,039
That's alright, Master P'Aya.

366
00:19:58,680 --> 00:20:00,376
I still have matters to
attend to for Master P'Eng.

367
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:01,759
I'm fine standing.

368
00:20:03,079 --> 00:20:04,439
Is P'Eng not back yet?

369
00:20:04,519 --> 00:20:05,279
No, sir.

370
00:20:05,359 --> 00:20:07,119
Master P'Eng will likely be late.

371
00:20:07,799 --> 00:20:09,440
Still with that boy, is he?

372
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:11,960
Yes.

373
00:20:15,279 --> 00:20:16,400
This thing between them...

374
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:17,480
What do you make of it?

375
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:21,320
It's not my place to interfere
in the Young Master's affairs.

376
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:22,680
I simply follow orders.

377
00:20:23,240 --> 00:20:24,400
Come now.

378
00:20:25,559 --> 00:20:27,759
You know how P'Eng is.

379
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:30,079
He's brilliant at everything he does,

380
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:32,440
until feelings get involved.

381
00:20:33,079 --> 00:20:35,039
The moment he catches feelings,

382
00:20:35,119 --> 00:20:36,519
he throws all caution to the wind.

383
00:20:38,359 --> 00:20:41,039
It's not that I'm against
them being together.

384
00:20:41,119 --> 00:20:43,360
It's just that you know P'Eng's nature.

385
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:44,679
He's terribly stubborn.

386
00:20:44,759 --> 00:20:46,959
When he's obsessed with a
new toy, no one can touch it.

387
00:20:47,839 --> 00:20:49,319
But the second he loses interest,

388
00:20:50,279 --> 00:20:52,119
he tosses them aside
without a second thought.

389
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,080
He can be utterly ruthless.

390
00:20:54,839 --> 00:20:55,960
Don't you agree?

391
00:21:01,559 --> 00:21:04,160
That boy seems quite
innocent and kind-hearted.

392
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:06,559
We shouldn't let an innocent kid get hurt.

393
00:21:07,559 --> 00:21:08,559
So,

394
00:21:09,559 --> 00:21:12,999
find an opportunity to
end things between them.

395
00:21:13,079 --> 00:21:17,160
It's for the best... for
him, and for the company.

396
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:19,240
What do you think?

397
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:24,920
How would you like me to handle it?

398
00:21:30,279 --> 00:21:31,359
First of all,

399
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:34,439
hear people out and
understand what they want

400
00:21:34,519 --> 00:21:36,200
before you decide how to react.

401
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:38,759
Don't immediately get so defensive.

402
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:40,039
Try being a little gentler.

403
00:21:41,119 --> 00:21:42,119
Gentle?

404
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:47,279
The word "gentle" isn't
even in my vocabulary.

405
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:51,880
Yes, it is.

406
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:54,320
I've seen the way you
treat Xiaotong and Xiaoya.

407
00:21:55,759 --> 00:21:56,759
Really?

408
00:21:57,960 --> 00:21:59,000
That counts as gentle?

409
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:00,800
Yeah.

410
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:02,759
That's exactly what
being gentle feels like.

411
00:22:03,720 --> 00:22:04,640
Tell you what,

412
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:05,896
why not try treating everyone else

413
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:07,640
like they're kids, too?

414
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:08,959
Give it a shot.

415
00:22:09,039 --> 00:22:10,039
It just might work.

416
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:14,480
Alright.

417
00:22:15,359 --> 00:22:16,359
I promise you.

418
00:22:16,920 --> 00:22:18,320
I'll do my best to be

419
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:19,400
a gentler person.

420
00:22:31,799 --> 00:22:33,279
Wait, you haven't had dinner yet?

421
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:37,559
I was so busy looking for
you, I completely forgot to eat.

422
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:48,200
So, this scooter...

423
00:22:48,759 --> 00:22:50,039
is mine now, right?

424
00:22:50,799 --> 00:22:51,799
Yep.

425
00:23:00,799 --> 00:23:01,799
This scooter

426
00:23:02,839 --> 00:23:03,960
belongs to you now.

427
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:09,400
We don't have anything fancy at my place,

428
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:11,759
but if you come back with
me, I can whip up something

429
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:14,319
to tide you over.

430
00:23:21,759 --> 00:23:23,839
So when you say you "follow orders,"

431
00:23:24,599 --> 00:23:26,519
you only mean P'Eng's orders.

432
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:28,320
Is that it?

433
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:29,400
I wouldn't dare.

434
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:33,360
I just feel this matter
is far too personal.

435
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:35,640
It's best to let Master
P'Eng handle it himself.

436
00:23:35,720 --> 00:23:37,479
Besides, I'm not clever enough

437
00:23:37,559 --> 00:23:38,640
to come up with a good way

438
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:39,920
to break them up quickly.

439
00:23:43,240 --> 00:23:45,440
You grew up with P'Eng.

440
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,719
You must know him inside and out.

441
00:23:47,799 --> 00:23:49,360
Given your age

442
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:50,440
and experience,

443
00:23:51,039 --> 00:23:53,720
there's no way you can't
figure out how to end this.

444
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:05,480
By the way,

445
00:24:06,359 --> 00:24:08,159
your parents are over
in Norway, aren't they?

446
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:09,799
I trust they're doing well?

447
00:24:10,839 --> 00:24:11,920
Thanks to you,

448
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:13,000
they are doing very well.

449
00:24:14,440 --> 00:24:16,839
I really envy them for
having such a devoted son.

450
00:24:18,559 --> 00:24:21,279
Father sent them to the mines in Norway.

451
00:24:22,039 --> 00:24:23,559
That must have been years ago.

452
00:24:24,680 --> 00:24:26,240
You must miss them terribly.

453
00:24:28,920 --> 00:24:30,119
If you miss them that much,

454
00:24:30,839 --> 00:24:32,440
I can always send you to Norway, too.

455
00:24:33,839 --> 00:24:35,239
You're all grown up now, after all.

456
00:24:36,119 --> 00:24:37,839
It's time you fulfilled your duty as a son.

457
00:24:38,599 --> 00:24:40,239
It's the least our family can do for you.

458
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:49,079
You catch my drift, don't you?

459
00:24:49,799 --> 00:24:50,799
Yes.

460
00:24:51,359 --> 00:24:53,479
I grew up right alongside Master P'Eng.

461
00:24:53,559 --> 00:24:54,896
Even though he's the young master,

462
00:24:54,920 --> 00:24:56,160
in my eyes,

463
00:24:56,240 --> 00:24:57,960
he's no different from family.

464
00:24:58,799 --> 00:25:00,400
I once promised the late master

465
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:03,080
that I would take good care of
this family and the young masters.

466
00:25:03,759 --> 00:25:05,400
However, I also believe

467
00:25:05,480 --> 00:25:06,800
that even without me,

468
00:25:06,880 --> 00:25:08,759
you both will do just fine.

469
00:25:35,480 --> 00:25:36,680
All we have left is noodles.

470
00:25:37,519 --> 00:25:38,800
It'll have to do for now.

471
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:39,880
Works for me.

472
00:25:42,119 --> 00:25:43,400
Pao Bei!

473
00:25:43,480 --> 00:25:44,360
You're back!

474
00:25:44,440 --> 00:25:45,679
And P'Eng is here, too!

475
00:25:45,759 --> 00:25:46,160
Hey.

476
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:47,039
Xiaotong, Xiaoya.

477
00:25:47,119 --> 00:25:48,199
Come give me a hug.

478
00:25:48,279 --> 00:25:49,279
Come here.

479
00:26:01,079 --> 00:26:02,919
What's the big secret
I'm not allowed to hear?

480
00:26:05,720 --> 00:26:06,199
Go on.

481
00:26:06,279 --> 00:26:07,279
Okay.

482
00:26:08,039 --> 00:26:09,039
Let's go.

483
00:26:12,599 --> 00:26:13,239
What are you up to?

484
00:26:13,319 --> 00:26:14,439
Why so secretive?

485
00:26:14,519 --> 00:26:16,239
Finish eating first,

486
00:26:16,319 --> 00:26:17,696
then let's go out for some fresh air.

487
00:26:17,720 --> 00:26:18,640
You'll find out soon enough.

488
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:19,720
Stop asking.

489
00:26:34,920 --> 00:26:36,199
Seriously though,

490
00:26:36,279 --> 00:26:37,799
you guys should all move in with me.

491
00:26:38,759 --> 00:26:40,279
That way, I can take good care of you.

492
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:47,240
I still prefer sitting right
here, looking at the stars.

493
00:26:48,880 --> 00:26:49,960
The stars?

494
00:26:52,480 --> 00:26:53,480
Can't you see the stars

495
00:26:53,559 --> 00:26:54,559
from my place, too?

496
00:26:56,160 --> 00:26:57,319
It's not the same.

497
00:26:59,359 --> 00:27:01,079
Have you ever heard that lyric,

498
00:27:01,720 --> 00:27:03,759
"Stars are a poor man's pearls"?

499
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:05,680
Never heard of it.

500
00:27:05,720 --> 00:27:06,720
What song is that from?

501
00:27:07,240 --> 00:27:09,039
It's a song I really love

502
00:27:09,119 --> 00:27:11,279
called "Silk Road."

503
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,480
When the lyrics say

504
00:27:14,359 --> 00:27:16,680
"stars are a poor man's pearls,"

505
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:21,160
I guess this is the exact feeling it means.

506
00:27:26,039 --> 00:27:27,479
I can give you way more

507
00:27:27,559 --> 00:27:28,999
than just pearls.

508
00:27:29,079 --> 00:27:30,479
Anything you like,

509
00:27:30,559 --> 00:27:31,559
anything you want.

510
00:27:32,359 --> 00:27:35,359
Don't you want a better life than this?

511
00:27:37,759 --> 00:27:39,480
I want that more than anyone.

512
00:27:40,400 --> 00:27:41,559
But I feel like.

513
00:27:42,519 --> 00:27:44,440
I need time to adjust.

514
00:27:46,480 --> 00:27:47,720
If things change too fast,

515
00:27:48,480 --> 00:27:49,959
it'll feel like I'm abandoning

516
00:27:50,039 --> 00:27:51,400
who I used to be.

517
00:27:56,119 --> 00:27:57,119
Forget it.

518
00:27:57,160 --> 00:27:58,519
I'm just being weird.

519
00:27:59,079 --> 00:28:00,639
I don't blame you for feeling that way.

520
00:28:09,480 --> 00:28:10,960
I'm realizing.

521
00:28:12,599 --> 00:28:16,160
I've never truly stepped into your world.

522
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:21,279
A lot of what you said today

523
00:28:21,359 --> 00:28:22,440
really surprised me.

524
00:28:23,079 --> 00:28:24,720
I used to just see you as a kid.

525
00:28:26,359 --> 00:28:27,440
I had no idea

526
00:28:28,720 --> 00:28:31,200
you were so mature for your age.

527
00:28:34,920 --> 00:28:36,640
When it comes to emotions,

528
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:39,519
I feel like you could be my teacher.

529
00:28:41,680 --> 00:28:42,920
You're just realizing that now?

530
00:28:43,599 --> 00:28:44,599
Well then,

531
00:28:45,279 --> 00:28:46,839
how about I be your relationship coach,

532
00:28:47,720 --> 00:28:49,240
and you teach me how to make money?

533
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:51,600
Or better yet,

534
00:28:51,680 --> 00:28:53,519
I could come work at Yingyu Group.

535
00:28:55,240 --> 00:28:57,759
I want to be able to help you out, too.

536
00:29:02,079 --> 00:29:04,200
Don't ever hold yourself back for me.

537
00:29:06,200 --> 00:29:07,719
You just keep moving forward,

538
00:29:07,799 --> 00:29:08,880
and as for me,

539
00:29:10,119 --> 00:29:12,440
I'll work hard to catch up to you.

540
00:29:20,279 --> 00:29:21,799
Pao Bei, we're done!

541
00:29:22,759 --> 00:29:24,080
Go ahead and bring it out.

542
00:29:24,160 --> 00:29:26,080
Close your eyes!

543
00:29:26,160 --> 00:29:27,400
Close my eyes?

544
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:31,000
He's definitely your brother, Pao Bei.

545
00:29:31,599 --> 00:29:32,599
Here!

546
00:29:36,119 --> 00:29:37,200
You can open your eyes now!

547
00:29:48,720 --> 00:29:49,720
Who's all

548
00:29:50,839 --> 00:29:51,839
on here?

549
00:29:52,359 --> 00:29:53,560
It's the four of us,

550
00:29:53,640 --> 00:29:54,320
plus A Pong,

551
